<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mfecane</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mfecane was a period of widespread warfare, migration and state formation in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in the early nineteenth century, associated with the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> kingdom under Shaka. It sent waves of armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> groups northwards across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a>. Their incursions in the 1820s and 1830s contributed to the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mfecane.jpg" alt="Mfecane" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Departure_of_the_Fingoes-1840.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
